{"schema":1,"function":"invgamma_ppf","description":"Inverse gamma distribution quantile function, the x with Q(a, 1/x) = p (shape a, rate 1); the reciprocal of the gamma quantile at 1 - p","inputs":["a","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":405,"tolerance":{"rel":2e-13,"reason":"As for gamma_ppf: the quantile is x = 1/t with t = exp(L), and rounding L (or 1/a, which multiplies it in the gamma lower tail) to a double changes x by |log x| times 2^-53. The largest |log x| at a finite, normal quantile on this grid is 691.3 (a = 0.01, p = 0.999, x = 1.8e300), so up to 7.7e-14 is unavoidable; 2e-13 allows 2.6x that and matches gamma_ppf. Quantiles above the largest double are tagged overflow. SciPy fails 11 of the 15 points with p = 5e-324 (5.5e-13 to 1.6e-4 off; it is right at a = 1, 1.5, 2 and 3) and no other point"},"grid":"a in {0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 150, 1e3, 1e4} x the gamma_ppf probabilities p in {0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, and the doubles nearest 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15, 1}; the quantile is 0 at p = 0 (the end of the support) and p = 1 is tagged pole (+inf); for small a the upper quantiles are above the largest double","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.invgamma.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
